--TEST--
a field that a retrieval's result is read by is refused, because the checker records no link from that read to the declaration, and a rename that missed it would break the program, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
attribute Index on class { col<|>umns: string }

#[Index(columns: "email")]
class Order {}

$index = Core\Attributes::get<Index>(Order::constructor);
echo $index?->columns ?? "";
--REQUEST--
rename to=fields
--EXPECT--
refused: `case.nvs` reads `->columns` on line 8. Rename cannot tell if that value comes from this attribute, so `Index::columns` cannot be renamed.
